  {
   "id": "1q1jm3-GAgAJ",
   "from": "Irene Duch Latorre",
   "author": "5caaf011fe45f4d4",
   "date": "2019-09-06T03:30:46Z",
   "subject": "Determining interval cutpoints for the distance histogram",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\">Dear colleagues,</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\">I hope this email finds you well. We have decided to compare density estimates calculated using Conventional Distance Sampling with those obtained with the Kelker method for our project. I acknowledge this email list is intended to share thoughts about the distance sampling technique, but I though some of you may also have expertise in the (related) Kelker method.  <br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\">My question is: How do you choose the interval cutpoints for the distance histogram? From my understanding, it is subjective, but I would appreciate any insight or experience you can share.</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\">Thank you for your help and for your time. I am looking forward to your reply.</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\">Best regards,</div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\"><br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\">Irene<br></div><div class=\"gmail_default\" style=\"font-family:georgia,serif;font-size:small;color:#000000\"><br></div><div><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(0,255,0)\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">Irene Duch-Latorre</span><br>\r\n</span></span></span></font></div><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">\r\n</span></span></font><div><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span style=\"background-color:rgb(0,255,0)\"></span>PhD Student, Department of Anthropology, </span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">UW-Madison</span></span> <br> <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><a href=\"https://strierlab.anthropology.wisc.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://strierlab.anthropology.wisc.edu/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792473901234000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2F8VdT0BkMfL3o46LQQ8fQ\">Strier Lab – Primate Behavioral Ecology and Conservation</a></span><br></span></span></font> <font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia,serif\"><a href=\"https://www.proyectowashu.org/\" title=\"https://www.proyectowashu.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.proyectowashu.org/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792473901234000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1fXwSvoC_LRiU13iD3z4LT\"><span style=\"color:rgb(189,19,152)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">Proyecto Washu</span></span></a></span></font></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n"
    ]
