  {
   "id": "l8HVfwKGAwAJ",
   "from": "David Lawrence Miller",
   "author": "350dad0a615d36db",
   "date": "2019-09-09T09:33:04Z",
   "subject": "Re: [distance-sampling] Determining interval cutpoints for the distance histogram",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi Irene, hi listfolk,\r<br>\r<br>Not sure if you mean choosing cutpoints to use to analyse the data as \r<br>grouped distances or just for displaying the fitted detection function?\r<br>\r<br>In both cases it&#39;s worth bearing in mind that you care more about what \r<br>the detection function is doing close to 0 distance (this also has a \r<br>larger effect on what your estimate of detection probability is).\r<br>\r<br>So for display, having more, smaller bins near zero (and through to the \r<br>shoulder of the function) and fewer, larger bins at larger distances \r<br>lets you see how well the function is fitting the data where it matters.\r<br>\r<br>For fitting group distances there is quite a lot of information from p \r<br>259 onwards in the 2001 Introduction to Distance Sampling book by \r<br>Buckland et al.\r<br>\r<br>Hope that helps!\r<br>\r<br>best,\r<br>--dave\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "\r<br>\r<br>On 06/09/2019 04:30, Irene Duch Latorre wrote:\r<br>&gt; Dear colleagues,\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; I hope this email finds you well. We have decided to compare density \r<br>&gt; estimates calculated using Conventional Distance Sampling with those \r<br>&gt; obtained with the Kelker method for our project. I acknowledge this \r<br>&gt; email list is intended to share thoughts about the distance sampling \r<br>&gt; technique, but I though some of you may also have expertise in the \r<br>&gt; (related) Kelker method.\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; My question is: How do you choose the interval cutpoints for the \r<br>&gt; distance histogram? From my understanding, it is subjective, but I would \r<br>&gt; appreciate any insight or experience you can share.\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Thank you for your help and for your time. I am looking forward to your \r<br>&gt; reply.\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Best regards,\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Irene\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; Irene Duch-Latorre\r<br>&gt; PhD Student, Department of Anthropology, UW-Madison\r<br>&gt; Strier Lab – Primate Behavioral Ecology and Conservation \r<br>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "&gt; &lt;<a href=\"https://strierlab.anthropology.wisc.edu/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://strierlab.anthropology.wisc.edu/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792473901235000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3yFeGoJiiQsjr89TH-Dvlo\">https://strierlab.anthropology.wisc.edu/</a>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Proyecto Washu &lt;<a href=\"https://www.proyectowashu.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.proyectowashu.org/&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792473901235000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3bD-C3K79xbXFAgVhGDKkz\">https://www.proyectowashu.org/</a>&gt;\r<br>&gt; \r<br>&gt; -- \r<br>&gt; You received this message because you are subscribed to the Google \r<br>&gt; Groups &quot;distance-sampling&quot; group.\r<br>&gt; To unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send \r<br>&gt; an email to <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance-sampl...@googlegroups.com</a> \r<br>&gt; &lt;mailto:<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">distance-sampl...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt;.\r<br>&gt; To view this discussion on the web visit \r<br>&gt; <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/distance-sampling/CAFoQvL_7pvWejs5P%2BrcTftdeg-Z9yMF7pjx2vJLe%3DLoXwZKXoA%40mail.gmail.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/distance-sampling/CAFoQvL_7pvWejs5P%252BrcTftdeg-Z9yMF7pjx2vJLe%253DLoXwZKXoA%2540mail.gmail.com&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792473901235000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1i3aCWdbJNo1e58I9QBO0p\">https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/distance-sampling/CAFoQvL_7pvWejs5P%2BrcTftdeg-Z9yMF7pjx2vJLe%3DLoXwZKXoA%40mail.gmail.com</a> \r<br>&gt; &lt;<a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/distance-sampling/CAFoQvL_7pvWejs5P%2BrcTftdeg-Z9yMF7pjx2vJLe%3DLoXwZKXoA%40mail.gmail.com?utm_medium=email&amp;utm_source=footer\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl